Changelog: 13-11-2026 21:54:15

Fixed. The app's tests pass again (58 of 155 failed or stopped in their fixtures since the suite got its own tooling
back), and tools/ci-local.sh runs them. The files of a suite with tools of its own, which the tests copy into their
fixtures, are back in tests/fixtures/windows-suite/. The fixtures' suites without a TAG_PREFIX are read with this
checkout's manifest tools, which ask for ps5-: in the tests they take a tag with or without it (tests/conftest.py),
and the fixtures' apps name a category, as this suite's apps.toml must. The fixtures hold the suite's own core
(core/bazzite_console_core, what the tool looks at for a core change) instead of nexus_core, the test of a suite's
name and icon reads this checkout, and the tag button's test expects the hint the button gives ("Nothing to
publish"). The tool itself is unchanged, apart from one docstring that named the wrong core folder.

